IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-organs-suicide.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII: sections 240.1 (trafficking in human organs), 241 (counselling or aiding suicide),
-- 242 (neglect to obtain assistance in childbirth) and 243 (concealing body of child). (Sections 241.1 to 241.4 are in ccc8-part8-maid.l4.)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). Offences answer JUST TRUE or NOTHING (M1); an exemption ("No person commits ... if") answers JUST FALSE when it applies.
-- The meanings of "medical assistance in dying", "medical practitioner", "nurse practitioner" and "pharmacist" are those of section 241.1: they enter as inputs `by s 241(7)`.

§ `Section 240.1 -- Trafficking in human organs`

-- src:4613 | 240.1 (1) Everyone commits an offence who
-- src:4614 | (a) obtains an organ to be transplanted into their body or into the body of another person, knowing that the person from whom it was removed or a person lawfully authorized to consent on behalf of the person from whom it was removed did not give informed consent to the removal, or being reckless as to whether or not such consent was given;
-- src:4615 | (b) carries out, participates in or facilitates the removal of an organ from the body of another person, knowing that the person from whom it was removed or a person lawfully authorized to consent on behalf of the person from whom it was removed did not give informed consent to the removal, or being reckless as to whether or not such consent was given; or
-- src:4616 | (c) does anything in connection with the removal of an organ from the body of another person on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with the person who removes the organ, knowing that the person from whom it was removed or a person lawfully authorized to consent on behalf of the person from whom it was removed did not give informed consent to the removal, or being reckless as to whether or not such consent was given.
@ref s 240.1(1) (src:4613-4616)
DECLARE `s 240.1(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 240.1(1)(a) obtains an organ to be transplanted into their body or into the body of another person`
    `s 240.1(1)(b) carries out, participates in or facilitates the removal of an organ from the body of another person`
    `s 240.1(1)(c) does anything in connection with the removal of an organ from the body of another person on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with the person who removes the organ`

@ref s 240.1(1) (src:4613-4616)
GIVEN act IS A `s 240.1(1) act`
      `the person knows that the person from whom the organ was removed, or a person lawfully authorized to consent on their behalf, did not give informed consent to the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reckless as to whether or not such consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` MEANS
    IF `the person knows that the person from whom the organ was removed, or a person lawfully authorized to consent on their behalf, did not give informed consent to the removal` OR `the person is reckless as to whether or not such consent was given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who (a) obtains an organ ..., knowing that ... did not give informed consent to the removal, or being reckless as to whether or not such consent was given" (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4618 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who obtains or participates in or facilitates the obtaining of an organ from the body of another person for the purposes of having that organ transplanted into their body or the body of another person, knowing that it was obtained for consideration or being reckless as to whether or not it was obtained for consideration.
@ref s 240.1(2) (src:4618-4618)
GIVEN `the person obtains, or participates in or facilitates the obtaining of, an organ from the body of another person for the purposes of having that organ transplanted into their body or the body of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was obtained for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reckless as to whether or not it was obtained for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240.1(2) the person commits the offence of obtaining an organ for consideration` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains, or participates in or facilitates the obtaining of, an organ from the body of another person for the purposes of having that organ transplanted into their body or the body of another person` AND (`the person knows that it was obtained for consideration` OR `the person is reckless as to whether or not it was obtained for consideration`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who obtains or participates in or facilitates the obtaining of an organ ... knowing that it was obtained for consideration or being reckless" (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4620 | (3) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 240.1(3) (src:4620-4620)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 240.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits an offence under subsection (2), by s 240.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 240.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person commits an offence under subsection (2), by s 240.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an indictable offence" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 240.1(3) (src:4620-4620)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 240.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 240.1(3) (src:4620-4620)
`s 240.1(3) the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 240.1(3) (src:4620-4620)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 240.1(3) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 240.1(3) the limb`

§ `Section 241 -- Counselling or aiding suicide`

-- src:4640 | (7) In this section, medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner and pharmacist have the same meanings as in section 241.1.
@ref s 241(7) (src:4640-4640)
GIVEN `the answer of section 241.1 for the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` MEANS `the answer of section 241.1 for the term`   -- the same answer as section 241.1 gives for medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or pharmacist

-- src:4638 | (6) For greater certainty, the exemption set out in any of subsections (2) to (5) applies even if the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about any fact that is an element of the exemption.
@ref s 241(6) (src:4638-4638)
GIVEN `the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` MEANS
    IF `the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the exemption set out in any of subsections (2) to (5) applies even if the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about any fact that is an element of the exemption"

-- src:4624 | 241 (1) Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, whether suicide ensues or not,
-- src:4625 | (a) counsels a person to die by suicide or abets a person in dying by suicide; or
-- src:4626 | (b) aids a person to die by suicide.
@ref s 241(1) (src:4624-4626)
GIVEN `whether suicide ensues or not, the person counsels a person to die by suicide or abets a person in dying by suicide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whether suicide ensues or not, the person aids a person to die by suicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `whether suicide ensues or not, the person counsels a person to die by suicide or abets a person in dying by suicide` OR `whether suicide ensues or not, the person aids a person to die by suicide`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, whether suicide ensues or not, (a) ... or (b) ..." (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 241(1) (src:4624-4626)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 241(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 241(1) (src:4624-4626)
`s 241(1) the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 241(1) (src:4624-4626)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 241(1) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 241(1) the limb`

-- src:4628 | (2) No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 241(2) (src:4628-4628)
GIVEN `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 241(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person provides a person with medical assistance in dying, by s 241(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 241(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person provides a person with medical assistance in dying, by s 241(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`it is in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if" (the text says nothing of a practitioner who does not provide MAID in accordance with section 241.2)

-- src:4630 | (3) No person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 241(3) (src:4630-4630)
GIVEN `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying` AND (`it is in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything for the purpose of aiding"

-- src:4632 | (4) No pharmacist who dispenses a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if the pharmacist dispenses the substance further to a prescription that is written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 241(4) (src:4632-4632)
GIVEN `the person is a pharmacist, by s 241(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pharmacist dispenses a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pharmacist dispenses it further to a prescription that is written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a pharmacist, by s 241(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the pharmacist dispenses a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` AND (`the pharmacist dispenses it further to a prescription that is written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No pharmacist who dispenses a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if the pharmacist dispenses the substance further to a prescription that is written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No pharmacist who dispenses a substance ... commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if"

-- src:4634 | (5) No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything, at another person’s explicit request, for the purpose of aiding that other person to self-administer a substance that has been prescribed for that other person as part of the provision of medical assist­ance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 241(5) (src:4634-4634)
GIVEN `the person does anything, at another person's explicit request, for the purpose of aiding that other person to self-administer a substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substance has been prescribed for that other person as part of the provision of medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the person does anything, at another person's explicit request, for the purpose of aiding that other person to self-administer a substance` AND (`the substance has been prescribed for that other person as part of the provision of medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 241(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything, at another person's explicit request, for the purpose of aiding that other person to self-administer a substance that has been prescribed for that other person as part of the provision of medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything, at another person's explicit request"

-- src:4636 | (5.1) For greater certainty, no social worker, psychologist, psychiatrist, therapist, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or other health care professional commits an offence if they provide information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241(5.1) (src:4636-4636)
GIVEN `the person is a social worker, psychologist, psychiatrist, therapist, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or other health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(5.1) the health care professional commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a social worker, psychologist, psychiatrist, therapist, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or other health care professional` AND `the person provides information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For greater certainty, no social worker, psychologist, psychiatrist, therapist, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or other health care professional commits an offence if they provide information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an offence if they provide information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying"

§ `Sections 242 and 243 -- Neglect in child-birth and concealing dead body`

-- src:4792 | 242 A female person who, being pregnant and about to be delivered, with intent that the child shall not live or with intent to conceal the birth of the child, fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery is, if the child is permanently injured as a result of the failure or dies immediately before, during or in a short time after birth, as a result of the failure, guilty of
-- src:4793 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:4794 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 242 (src:4792-4794)
GIVEN `the person is a female person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she is pregnant and about to be delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she acts with intent that the child shall not live` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she acts with intent to conceal the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is permanently injured as a result of the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child dies immediately before, during or in a short time after birth, as a result of the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a female person` AND `she is pregnant and about to be delivered` AND (`she acts with intent that the child shall not live` OR `she acts with intent to conceal the birth of the child`) AND `she fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery` AND (`the child is permanently injured as a result of the failure` OR `the child dies immediately before, during or in a short time after birth, as a result of the failure`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a female person` AND `she is pregnant and about to be delivered` AND (`she acts with intent that the child shall not live` OR `she acts with intent to conceal the birth of the child`) AND `she fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, if the child is permanently injured as a result of the failure or dies immediately before, during or in a short time after birth, as a result of the failure, guilty of" (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A female person who, being pregnant and about to be delivered, with intent that the child shall not live or with intent to conceal the birth of the child, fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery"

@ref s 242 (src:4792-4794)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 242 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 242(a) (src:4793-4793)
`s 242(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 242 (src:4792-4794)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 242 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 242(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4796 | 243 Every person who in any manner disposes of the dead body of a child, with intent to conceal the fact that its mother has been delivered of it, whether the child died before, during or after birth, is guilty of
-- src:4797 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:4798 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 243 (src:4796-4798)
-- "whether the child died before, during or after birth": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none.
GIVEN `the person in any manner disposes of the dead body of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to conceal the fact that its mother has been delivered of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243 the person commits the offence of concealing the body of a child` MEANS
    IF `the person in any manner disposes of the dead body of a child` AND `the person acts with intent to conceal the fact that its mother has been delivered of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who in any manner disposes of the dead body of a child, with intent to conceal the fact that its mother has been delivered of it ... is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 243 (src:4796-4798)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 243 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 243(a) (src:4797-4797)
`s 243(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 243 (src:4796-4798)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 243 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 243(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
